    feat(metrics): DF-2026-19 read-side recall counter + daily rollup + zero-day alert
    
    Adds MCP-boundary recall telemetry with crash-safe JSONL append records, a seven-day-capable rollup CLI with explicit numerator/denominator rates, and a health-gated zero-non-empty-pack alert that appends foreman-readable rows. The default counter is derived beside the configured namespaces directory and can be overridden with DUCKBRAIN_RECALL_METRICS_PATH; health comparison uses health.jsonl or DUCKBRAIN_RECALL_HEALTH_FILE and identifies GET /health status=200.
    
    Evidence: targeted Vitest 3/3 passed; TypeScript check passed; prettier passed for all code files; seven-day seeded rollup and forced-empty healthy-day alert produced /tmp/df2026-19-rollup.txt, with checker exit 1 and alert output verified. Full pnpm test:run reached 242/243 files and 2029/2030 tests; one pre-existing timeout remained in src/http/namespace-warmup-aug096.test.ts (concurrency knob test, 15s timeout).
    
